From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 17:01:46 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 101/148] feat(refinery): add merge-batch.sh select and stack
 (inert) with a real-repo suite (gcp-l8td.8)

D1.1 of the refinery batch merge (design on gcp-l8td.7). One patrol iteration
will be able to land several assigned beads behind a single gate run; this adds
the first half of the mechanics as a checked-in script so the agent never
hand-renders a batch lane. It is ADDITIVE and INERT: no formula step calls it
until the wiring bead (gcp-l8td.10), and `land` is gcp-l8td.9.

merge-batch.sh sources merge-push.sh in source-only mode and reuses
resolve_config, resolve_merge_strategy, resolve_approval_required and the
merge-state helpers, so a member is eligible by the lane's own rules.
- select --head <id> --max <K> prints the head plus a prefix of find-work's
  assignee scan (same sort, never --limit=1), cut at K and at the first
  ineligible bead. K is forced to 1 when the approval gate resolves ON, and an
  unreadable config resolves it ON. The head is printed even when it is itself
  ineligible, in which case the batch is that one bead.
- stack extends the rebased head `temp` with members 2..k, rebasing each onto
  the current temp. It ends the batch at the first member that conflicts, is
  ineligible, or collapses to no change, and leaves that member's bead alone.
  A collapsed member that passes branch_already_landed is closed
  already_merged by the existing helper and stacking continues past it. It
  writes the manifest `$(git rev-parse --git-dir)/refinery-batch.json`
  (head, target, base, and per member id, branch, tip, commits, patch_id),
  which `land` will read. Any internal error resets temp to the head tip
  recorded at entry, writes a one-member manifest, prints WARN and exits 0:
  batching only ever shortens to the single-bead lane.

Two judgement calls inside the design's room. The head must pass the member
rules itself, since a head that would hand off as a pull request cannot ride a
direct batch. And stack's member list comes from --members, else the manifest's
members, else the head alone, because the design leaves the agent's hand-off of
select's list to stack open.

gastown/tests/test_refinery_merge_batch.sh runs 9 cases against real temp git
repos (a bare origin, a polecat clone, the refinery's clone) with a gc stub over
a fixture directory of beads: select order, truncation, approval, stack clean,
conflict between members, already landed, degrade, the script's invariants, and
the merge-push extraction. Mutating the script's sort key or its degrade reset
fails the suite.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
